# This branch carries only the update feed.
#
# A .gitignore here is a safety rail, not housekeeping: switching to this
# branch from main leaves main untracked and ignored files sitting in the
# working tree — .env among them. Without this file .env is untracked AND
# unignored here, so one "git add -A" on the wrong branch would publish a
# site DB password, APP_KEY and SMTP credentials to a public repository.

/.env
/config/
/core/
/modules/
/public/
/resources/
/storage/
/tools/
/docs/
/vendor/
/dist/
/composer.json
/composer.lock
/LICENSE
/SKILL.md
/NEXT-SESSION.md
